}
```

The implementation of PUT_SetContract makes an assumption that `x` exists in `arrList` at `index`, and the goal is to observe the changes to `arrList` and `x` after setting the value at `index` to `x`. If these changes meet the assumptions, the test is considered passed. 

The PexObserve.ValueForViewing lines are used to print out the values into the Visual Studio output console.

To run this test, you need to install the Pex, PexLib, NUnit, and NUnit3TestAdapter packages by either using the NuGet console (Tools > NuGet Package Manager > Package Manager Console) or by command line:

```commandline
Install-Package Pex
Install-Package PexLib
Install-Package NUnit
Install-Package NUnit3TestAdapter
```

The test can then be run through a Test Explorer or from the context menu.--------------------        Debug.Assert(Old_arrListIndexOfX >= -1, "@@@ index of x in old array list is more than or same as -1");

